WEBVTT

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:03.904
Linnaeus also gave us a ranked system of groups.

00:00:03.904 --> 00:00:08.345
Each group at any rank is called a taxon, and the plural is taxa.

00:00:09.058 --> 00:00:16.195
From broadest to most specific, the ranks are domain, kingdom, phylum, class, order, family, genus, and species.

00:00:16.195 --> 00:00:17.915
To remember the order, try:

00:00:17.915 --> 00:00:20.528
Dear King Philip Came Over For Good Soup.

00:00:21.228 --> 00:00:23.632
Here's how the house cat is classified.

00:00:23.632 --> 00:00:29.548
As you move down the ranks, each group gets smaller, and its members have more traits in common.
